1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,060
Dan, please buy four carrots, three tomatoes,
and one cucumber. The blue list is for my
salad.

2
00:00:08,310 --> 00:00:10,110
I am ready.

3
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:20,910
Six potatoes, two onions, and broccoli for my
soup. Yellow is mine.

4
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:23,560
Two colors. Two delicious plans.

5
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:32,300
Blue for salad.

6
00:00:32,550 --> 00:00:34,350
Yellow for soup.

7
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:38,720
I have both. My memory has plenty of room.

8
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:47,900
Should we check those together?

9
00:00:48,150 --> 00:00:50,550
I have an excellent memory.

10
00:00:50,800 --> 00:00:54,060
We can bring excellent eyes as well.

11
00:01:00,500 --> 00:01:02,900
Blue soup, yellow salad. Easy.

12
00:01:03,150 --> 00:01:05,120
That sounds backward, Dad.

13
00:01:05,370 --> 00:01:09,490
Then we will check the details at the stall.

14
00:01:15,500 --> 00:01:19,620
I will carry the bags and check the
vegetables.

15
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:24,420
I have the basket. Does broccoli need a seat
belt?

16
00:01:30,500 --> 00:01:32,300
Ready, team?

17
00:01:32,550 --> 00:01:35,810
Ready. Even our empty basket looks hungry.

18
00:01:36,060 --> 00:01:40,610
Then let us bring it back with the right
lunch.

19
00:01:45,500 --> 00:01:48,760
Vegetables, team. We need vegetables, not
surprises.

20
00:01:49,010 --> 00:01:51,840
The stand is on the right.

21
00:01:52,090 --> 00:01:54,920
The surprises may be there too.

22
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:05,050
Can you carry the basket, Dad? It is very
heavy.

23
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:07,270
But it is empty!

24
00:02:07,520 --> 00:02:10,780
I am saving my muscles for later.

25
00:02:15,500 --> 00:02:19,190
The bags can wait here while we choose.

26
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:22,270
And we keep the aisle clear.

27
00:02:22,520 --> 00:02:24,920
An organized beginning. I approve.

28
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,900
Ours has the blue handle.

29
00:02:33,150 --> 00:02:36,840
Good. We are not shopping for somebody else.

30
00:02:37,090 --> 00:02:40,780
Let us check the food just as carefully.

31
00:02:45,500 --> 00:02:47,300
Forty carrots?

32
00:02:47,550 --> 00:02:49,520
Four, Dad. Four carrots.

33
00:02:49,770 --> 00:02:53,890
Good catch. Forty would need their own
shopping cart.

34
00:03:00,500 --> 00:03:02,470
One, two, three, four.

35
00:03:02,720 --> 00:03:05,550
Four is much easier to carry.

36
00:03:05,800 --> 00:03:09,060
And exactly what the list asked for.

37
00:03:15,500 --> 00:03:18,330
Should we get a few extra?

38
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:20,550
We have four already.

39
00:03:20,800 --> 00:03:24,490
Then the others can stay for another family.

40
00:03:30,500 --> 00:03:34,620
Three ripe tomatoes. The tray will keep them
safe.

41
00:03:34,870 --> 00:03:36,840
Three tiny bowling balls?

42
00:03:37,090 --> 00:03:40,350
Only if you want tomato soup everywhere.

43
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:47,470
Three tomatoes, safely aboard.

44
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:50,550
Keep the heavy things underneath later.

45
00:03:50,800 --> 00:03:54,060
A first-class ticket for the soft passengers.

46
00:04:00,500 --> 00:04:04,190
We can make room before anything gets
squashed.

47
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:09,420
Good idea. The tomatoes should finish this
trip looking like tomatoes.

48
00:04:15,500 --> 00:04:18,760
Long, green, ready for salad. A cucumber!

49
00:04:19,010 --> 00:04:23,990
That is a zucchini. The cucumbers are in the
next crate.

50
00:04:24,240 --> 00:04:26,040
A useful introduction.

51
00:04:30,500 --> 00:04:33,330
This is the cucumber we need.

52
00:04:33,580 --> 00:04:38,130
Two green cousins. I checked the right name
this time.

53
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:40,780
And only one comes home.

54
00:04:45,500 --> 00:04:48,760
Shape helps, but the label helps too.

55
00:04:49,010 --> 00:04:51,840
I will use both next time.

56
00:04:52,090 --> 00:04:55,780
That gives your excellent memory a little
help.

57
00:05:00,500 --> 00:05:03,330
The yellow note is still hiding.

58
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:06,410
Then it deserves some fresh air.

59
00:05:06,660 --> 00:05:09,920
And a careful look at its heading.

60
00:05:15,500 --> 00:05:19,620
Six potatoes for the salad? That sounds very
crunchy.

61
00:05:19,870 --> 00:05:22,700
Maybe we should check the heading.

62
00:05:22,950 --> 00:05:25,780
Yes. Before we sort the bags.

63
00:05:30,500 --> 00:05:34,190
Six potatoes. One, two, three, four, five,
six.

64
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:36,240
Heavy passengers downstairs.

65
00:05:36,490 --> 00:05:39,750
And the tomatoes keep their safe seats.

66
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:49,190
The potatoes will not squash the tomatoes now.

67
00:05:49,440 --> 00:05:53,130
Good. At least their travel arrangements are
clear.

68
00:05:53,380 --> 00:05:56,640
We can make the lists clear too.

69
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:03,760
These onions are making me cry already.

70
00:06:04,010 --> 00:06:06,410
You have not cut them.

71
00:06:06,660 --> 00:06:09,490
Perhaps they heard my potato-salad plan.

72
00:06:15,500 --> 00:06:19,190
One onion, two onions. Which dish gets them?

73
00:06:19,440 --> 00:06:21,240
An excellent question.

74
00:06:21,490 --> 00:06:26,040
We can ask the notes when we open them
properly.

75
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:35,050
We can check before anything goes in the wrong
bag.

76
00:06:35,300 --> 00:06:37,700
That is a good plan.

77
00:06:37,950 --> 00:06:41,640
There is still plenty of time to ask.

78
00:06:45,500 --> 00:06:48,760
That broccoli looks like a tiny tree.

79
00:06:49,010 --> 00:06:52,270
A forest small enough for our basket.

80
00:06:52,520 --> 00:06:56,210
Then I will save it a window seat.

81
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:04,620
One head of broccoli. That is all we need.

82
00:07:04,870 --> 00:07:07,270
The forest has arrived safely.

83
00:07:07,520 --> 00:07:11,640
And the basket still has room for the rest.

84
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:20,480
Why is it a bell pepper if it does not ring?

85
00:07:20,730 --> 00:07:23,130
Perhaps it is on silent.

86
00:07:23,380 --> 00:07:26,640
That is very polite in a shop.

87
00:07:30,500 --> 00:07:34,620
The blue list asks for one red bell pepper.

88
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:39,420
Blue paper, red pepper. I will keep those
details separate.

89
00:07:39,670 --> 00:07:41,470
That will help.

90
00:07:45,500 --> 00:07:49,620
That one looks good. The skin is not damaged.

91
00:07:49,870 --> 00:07:52,270
And it has excellent manners.

92
00:07:52,520 --> 00:07:54,320
Still silent?

93
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:03,330
One red bell pepper, safely packed.

94
00:08:03,580 --> 00:08:05,380
Checked.

95
00:08:05,630 --> 00:08:09,320
A quiet ingredient and a very useful helper.

96
00:08:15,500 --> 00:08:19,190
Two ears of corn. Can they hear us?

97
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:22,270
Only if we speak very politely.

98
00:08:22,520 --> 00:08:24,320
Good morning, corn.

99
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:32,900
Two ears. Both look fresh.

100
00:08:33,150 --> 00:08:35,550
They came as a pair.

101
00:08:35,800 --> 00:08:39,490
Then let us keep their ride gentle too.

102
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,470
Two ears, safely aboard.

103
00:08:47,720 --> 00:08:49,690
Thank you for listening.

104
00:08:49,940 --> 00:08:52,770
They are our most patient passengers.

105
00:09:00,500 --> 00:09:02,470
A very tidy lettuce?

106
00:09:02,720 --> 00:09:06,840
That is cabbage. Our list asks for loose-leaf
lettuce.

107
00:09:07,090 --> 00:09:10,350
Then we need the less tidy one.

108
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:18,330
These leaves are loose and open.

109
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:20,980
Not a round cabbage ball.

110
00:09:21,230 --> 00:09:24,060
Right. One lettuce for the salad.

111
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:33,330
The lettuce gets the top seat.

112
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:36,410
Soft leaves need a gentle journey.

113
00:09:36,660 --> 00:09:40,350
Our basket is becoming a very considerate bus.

114
00:09:45,500 --> 00:09:47,300
One ingredient left.

115
00:09:47,550 --> 00:09:50,380
The little bag of green leaves.

116
00:09:50,630 --> 00:09:53,460
Then spinach is our final passenger.

117
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:03,330
Spinach. Is this the last passenger?

118
00:10:03,580 --> 00:10:05,980
Yes. One bag of spinach.

119
00:10:06,230 --> 00:10:09,490
Then the basket can stop taking reservations.

120
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:18,760
That is everything. Ten ingredient lines
checked.

121
00:10:19,010 --> 00:10:20,980
All the right vegetables.

122
00:10:21,230 --> 00:10:25,350
Now we can check which dish gets which ones.

123
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:35,050
Let us put them where we can see both
headings.

124
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:37,270
Blue salad. Yellow soup.

125
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:41,210
That is what they have said all morning.

126
00:10:45,500 --> 00:10:50,910
I put the dish names in the wrong places in my
head.

127
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:54,420
The vegetables are in the right place.

128
00:10:54,670 --> 00:10:57,500
And we can sort them correctly.

129
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:05,480
Maya, I remembered the colors backward. Blue
is your salad, right?

130
00:11:05,730 --> 00:11:11,570
Right. The blue list is my salad. You can
check it with me.

131
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:20,480
And yellow is my soup. Potatoes, onions,
broccoli, corn and spinach.

132
00:11:20,730 --> 00:11:26,140
The soup sounds much better now that it has
its own ingredients.

133
00:11:30,500 --> 00:11:33,330
I should have asked before guessing.

134
00:11:33,580 --> 00:11:37,700
You are asking now. We are glad to help.

135
00:11:37,950 --> 00:11:42,070
Bring our vegetables and our three helpers
home safely.

136
00:11:45,500 --> 00:11:49,620
Phone away. Two headings where we can see
them.

137
00:11:49,870 --> 00:11:52,270
That will make packing easier.

138
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:55,780
And make my memory work less hard.

139
00:12:00,500 --> 00:12:05,910
I mixed up the lists. Thank you for catching
it before packing.

140
00:12:06,160 --> 00:12:08,130
We are a team.

141
00:12:08,380 --> 00:12:12,500
Then let us give each dish its own bag.

142
00:12:15,500 --> 00:12:18,760
Blue bag beside the blue salad note.

143
00:12:19,010 --> 00:12:20,980
Yellow beside yellow soup.

144
00:12:21,230 --> 00:12:24,490
A filing system I can actually see.

145
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:33,760
Read the heading, then match the ingredients.

146
00:12:34,010 --> 00:12:36,840
Salad in blue. Soup in yellow.

147
00:12:37,090 --> 00:12:41,210
Now we can make the bags match the notes.

148
00:12:45,500 --> 00:12:49,190
Four carrots, three tomatoes, cucumber,
lettuce, red pepper.

149
00:12:49,440 --> 00:12:51,410
All for Maya's salad.

150
00:12:51,660 --> 00:12:54,060
The blue bag is ready.

151
00:13:00,500 --> 00:13:05,050
Potatoes, onions, broccoli, corn and spinach.
All for Nina's soup.

152
00:13:05,300 --> 00:13:08,130
The basket has finished its job.

153
00:13:08,380 --> 00:13:10,350
An excellent passenger service.

154
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:19,190
Blue salad. Yellow soup. Checked properly this
time.

155
00:13:19,440 --> 00:13:21,410
Both bags look right.

156
00:13:21,660 --> 00:13:24,920
Now we can pay for the vegetables.

157
00:13:30,500 --> 00:13:33,330
Eighteen dollars and fifty cents, please.

158
00:13:33,580 --> 00:13:35,380
Eighteen fifty.

159
00:13:35,630 --> 00:13:40,180
That matches our vegetables. We can check the
receipt too.

160
00:13:45,500 --> 00:13:47,900
Here you go. Twenty dollars.

161
00:13:48,150 --> 00:13:52,270
We should get one dollar and fifty cents back.

162
00:13:52,520 --> 00:13:57,070
Then I will check that as carefully as the
lists.

163
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:02,470
Here is your receipt.

164
00:14:02,720 --> 00:14:05,120
All ten ingredients are here.

165
00:14:05,370 --> 00:14:09,920
Good. Right vegetables, right total, and
nearly the right memory.

166
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:18,330
One dollar. Two quarters. One fifty.

167
00:14:18,580 --> 00:14:20,550
Small change, carefully checked.

168
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:23,200
The smallest passengers still count.

169
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:32,900
Receipt and change, both checked.

170
00:14:33,150 --> 00:14:35,550
And safely in my wallet.

171
00:14:35,800 --> 00:14:40,780
That is a better place for them than under the
lettuce.

172
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:47,300
Nothing left behind.

173
00:14:47,550 --> 00:14:50,810
Except the vegetables we did not buy.

174
00:14:51,060 --> 00:14:55,610
They can stay. We have exactly what our family
needs.

175
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,900
All three helpers. Both bags.

176
00:15:03,150 --> 00:15:05,550
And one safely empty basket.

177
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:09,490
It worked very hard without learning to cook.

178
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:19,190
Maya, your salad vegetables. Blue bag, blue
list.

179
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,240
And our helpers?

180
00:15:21,490 --> 00:15:24,750
All three. We checked that part too.

181
00:15:30,500 --> 00:15:34,620
My soup vegetables! Did the broccoli enjoy its
trip?

182
00:15:34,870 --> 00:15:37,700
It asked for a window seat.

183
00:15:37,950 --> 00:15:40,350
We offered very careful service.

184
00:15:45,500 --> 00:15:47,470
Exactly what we needed.

185
00:15:47,720 --> 00:15:51,410
And a funny story to go with it.

186
00:15:51,660 --> 00:15:56,210
I would like the next part to involve fewer
guesses.

187
00:16:00,500 --> 00:16:02,900
Hands first, after our trip.

188
00:16:03,150 --> 00:16:06,840
Then we can help with the safe jobs.

189
00:16:07,090 --> 00:16:10,350
Yes. Everybody has a part in lunch.

190
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:18,760
Even our well-traveled cucumber gets a wash.

191
00:16:19,010 --> 00:16:20,810
Especially that cucumber.

192
00:16:21,060 --> 00:16:26,470
Then the adults can do the cutting while you
set the table.

193
00:16:30,500 --> 00:16:33,760
I will take care of the napkins.

194
00:16:34,010 --> 00:16:37,270
And I will help with the vegetables.

195
00:16:37,520 --> 00:16:42,070
Careful hands and clear jobs. This part is
coming together.

196
00:16:45,500 --> 00:16:47,470
Shopping finished. Lunch finished?

197
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:51,840
We brought ingredients, Dan. They have not
cooked themselves.

198
00:16:52,090 --> 00:16:57,070
Then I am glad we left time for the next job.

199
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,470
The salad is ready.

200
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:05,980
And now the soup is cooked, too.

201
00:17:06,230 --> 00:17:10,780
Two dishes. One kitchen that has done some
excellent work.

202
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:17,900
Six places. Everybody has one.

203
00:17:18,150 --> 00:17:20,120
Even the smallest helper.

204
00:17:20,370 --> 00:17:25,780
Especially the smallest helper. And the basket
can rest on its chair.

205
00:17:30,500 --> 00:17:32,300
Salad for everyone.

206
00:17:32,550 --> 00:17:37,100
And cooked soup. Let it cool enough before you
taste.

207
00:17:37,350 --> 00:17:41,040
Lunch has finally arrived at the right seats.

208
00:17:45,500 --> 00:17:50,480
I felt embarrassed when I realized I mixed up
the lists.

209
00:17:50,730 --> 00:17:56,140
We helped because we love you. You help us
learn every day.

210
00:18:00,500 --> 00:18:03,330
You listened, checked, and tried again.

211
00:18:03,580 --> 00:18:06,840
And all our ingredients found their dishes.

212
00:18:07,090 --> 00:18:10,780
I had very good company along the way.

213
00:18:15,500 --> 00:18:19,190
Would forty carrots need their own dining
table?

214
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:22,270
Only if they came as guests.

215
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:25,780
Then four was a very considerate number.

216
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:33,760
A question helped more than another guess.

217
00:18:34,010 --> 00:18:36,840
Especially when the vegetables had ears.

218
00:18:37,090 --> 00:18:40,350
That was the polite part of shopping.

219
00:18:45,500 --> 00:18:50,050
Next time I am unsure, could you check with
me?

220
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:54,420
Of course. Asking for help is always welcome
here.

221
00:18:54,670 --> 00:18:57,500
That sounds like a useful plan.

222
00:19:00,500 --> 00:19:02,300
Blue salad.

223
00:19:02,550 --> 00:19:04,350
Yellow soup.

224
00:19:04,600 --> 00:19:10,440
Two notes that deserve to be read separately.
I will remember that part.

225
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:18,760
Tomorrow, we need fruit for a picnic.

226
00:19:19,010 --> 00:19:20,810
One list, please.

227
00:19:21,060 --> 00:19:23,030
One list. Two colors.

228
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:33,330
Tomorrow, we can choose fruit together.

229
00:19:33,580 --> 00:19:37,270
Three excellent helpers, and all six of us.

230
00:19:37,520 --> 00:19:40,780
That sounds like a very good team.

231
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:47,900
Two dishes. One happy family.

232
00:19:48,150 --> 00:19:50,550
Exactly the plan we wanted.

233
00:19:50,800 --> 00:19:54,490
And nobody left the basket at the market.
